WEBVTT

00:01:58.996 --> 00:02:00.156
It's so glamorous.

00:02:00.196 --> 00:02:03.316
This is how I became
a computational biologist.

00:02:04.316 --> 00:02:05.516
During that time,

00:02:05.516 --> 00:02:08.236
genomics and computing were coming of age.

00:02:08.276 --> 00:02:10.676
And I went on to do my masters

00:02:10.716 --> 00:02:13.796
combining biology and computers.

00:02:13.836 --> 00:02:14.996
During that time,

00:02:14.996 --> 00:02:16.796
I worked at Los Alamos National Lab

00:02:16.796 --> 00:02:19.316
in the theoretical biology
and biophysics group.

00:02:19.756 --> 00:02:23.516
And it was there I had my first encounter
with the supercomputer,

00:02:23.516 --> 00:02:25.196
and my mind was blown.

00:02:25.836 --> 00:02:27.876
With the power of supercomputing,

00:02:27.916 --> 00:02:32.116
which is basically thousands
of connected PCs on steroids,